.TH CHICCO 1 "2026-09" "chicco" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chicco \- local OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible rotation proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chicco
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chicco
serves one endpoint \(em chat completions, messages and embeddings \(em and
forwards each request to the next provider in
.IR chicco.yaml ,
rotating models and skipping providers that run out of quota, so that a single
stable endpoint fronts a pool of free-tier tokens.
.PP
Providers may be HTTP APIs or local CLI tools. Both OpenAI- and Anthropic-SDK
clients point straight at the address chicco serves, with no code changes.
Embeddings rotate across HTTP providers only, since CLI backends return text
rather than vectors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " PATH"
Path to the
.I chicco.yaml
config file (default
.IR chicco.yaml ).
.TP
.BI \-addr " ADDR"
Listen address, overriding
.IR chicco.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-state " PATH"
Where rotation state is kept across restarts (default
.IR chicco-state.json ).
.TP
.B \-headless
Disable the dashboard and log plainly to standard error.
.TP
.B \-check
Validate the config and exit. No server is started and no port is bound.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I chicco.yaml
Provider pool: endpoints, models and credentials.
.TP
.I chicco-state.json
Rotation state, so a restart does not go back to an exhausted provider.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Serve the pool on a fixed port:
.PP
.RS
.B chicco \-config chicco.yaml \-addr :41986
.RE
.PP
Then point an OpenAI client's base URL at
.IR http://127.0.0.1:41986/v1 .
.PP
Check a config without binding anything:
.PP
.RS
.B chicco \-check \-config chicco.yaml
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/chicco
